# Real downloaded PCIe/CXL sources and the chunked passage corpus built from them.
# Regenerate with: python scripts/fetch_corpus.py && python -m assistant.ingest
# (data/raw/ holds the real files fetch_corpus.py downloads from corpus_manifest.json's
# public URLs; data/corpus.jsonl is the chunked passages ingest.py builds from them. The
# CXL 1.1 Specification and its 2.0 errata are copyrighted by the CXL Consortium, not
# public domain, so this project never commits their extracted text.)
data/raw/
data/corpus.jsonl

# Real downloaded CSA CCM/CAIQ bundle and the question/control text extracted from it.
# Regenerate with: python -m scripts.fetch_caiq_corpus
# (caiq/data/raw/ holds the real downloaded bundle; caiq_questions.json/ccm_controls.json
# hold the real compiled question and control-specification text. CSA licenses the CCM
# free for internal use only, commercial use requires a license, so this project commits
# only caiq/manifest.json's taxonomy, caiq/data/evidence_library.json (this project's own
# synthetic evidence register, not CSA's text) and caiq/frozen_eval_set.json (ids and
# expected outcomes only, no question text).
caiq/data/raw/
caiq/data/caiq_questions.json
caiq/data/ccm_controls.json

# Real downloaded Cloudflare docs/blog pages and the chunked passage corpus built
# from them. Regenerate with: python -m comms_audit.scripts.fetch_corpus &&
# python -m comms_audit.ingest
# (comms_audit/data/raw/ holds the real extracted page text; comms_audit/data/corpus.jsonl
# is the chunked passages built from it. corpus_manifest.json (urls, titles, sha256
# checksums) is committed; the extracted text itself is not, the same precedent this
# project uses for the copyrighted CXL/PCI-SIG PDFs, even though Cloudflare's own
# robots.txt Content-Signal explicitly permits ai-input use of this content.)
comms_audit/data/raw/
comms_audit/data/corpus.jsonl
comms_audit/worker/dist/
